## D. Rolling-window statistics absorb a persistent shift (toy model of a rolling calculator)
One control series, true SD 1. 20 in-control runs establish stats. Persistent shift SE from run 1.
FIXED: mean/SD frozen after establishment. ROLLING: mean/SD recomputed over the last 20 results (all
results, including rejected ones) after each insert; each result's z uses the statistics in force before it.
Rules: 1_3s, 2_2s, 4_1s, 10x in the LIS-variant forms (>=, per series). Report P(detected by run k), 3000 reps.
SE=0.0 FIXED  : P(by run 5) 0.058, by 10 0.114, by 40 0.351; mean z over runs 26-30 when undetected: +0.01
