## E. Moving-average patient-based QC toy model (bias detection curve)
Synthetic patient stream: 90% N(140, 2.5), 10% N(133, 6) (a sodium-like mixture; synthetic).
Truncation 130-150; simple moving average of block N over retained results; symmetric control limits
calibrated on 400000 in-control results to ~1 false alarm per 10000 results. Bias added from result 1.
N=20, limit +/-2.55 around 139.73: bias 0.5: median 6000, p95 6000; bias 1.0: median 569, p95 2067; bias 2.0: median 41, p95 137; bias 3.0: median 21, p95 43 (patient results to detection, censored at 6000)
N=50, limit +/-1.71 around 139.72: bias 0.5: median 5448, p95 6000; bias 1.0: median 335, p95 1282; bias 2.0: median 52, p95 92; bias 3.0: median 51, p95 53 (patient results to detection, censored at 6000)
N=100, limit +/-1.16 around 139.71: bias 0.5: median 1576, p95 6000; bias 1.0: median 150, p95 479; bias 2.0: median 102, p95 105; bias 3.0: median 102, p95 104 (patient results to detection, censored at 6000)
(section E elapsed 2.8 s)
